---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.ts';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="Get in touch about an incorrect result, an unclear explanation, or a percentage calculator you would like to see added."
  path="/contact"
  h1="Contact"
  intro="Corrections, questions and suggestions are all welcome."
>
  <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6">
    <p class="eyebrow">Email</p>
    <p class="mt-2">
      <a
        href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}
        class="text-body break-all text-ink underline underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:opacity-70 sm:text-card-title"
        >{SITE.email}</a
      >
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose-site mt-10">
    <h2>Reporting an incorrect result</h2>
    <p>
      Accuracy matters more than anything else here, so these reports get looked at first. Including
      the following makes a problem much faster to reproduce:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which calculator you were using.</li>
      <li>The exact numbers you entered.</li>
      <li>The answer you got, and the answer you expected.</li>
      <li>Your browser and device, if the problem looks like a display issue.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Suggesting a calculator</h2>
    <p>
      If there is a percentage calculation you keep doing by hand, it is worth mentioning — a short
      description of the situation is more useful than a formula, because it explains what the tool
      would actually need to do.
    </p>

    <h2>What this address is not for</h2>
    <p>
      No personalised financial, tax, medical or legal advice can be offered, and homework cannot be
      completed on request. The <a href="/how-to-calculate-percentage">how-to guide</a> and the{' '}
      <a href="/percentage-formula">formula reference</a> explain the working behind every calculator
      on the site.
    </p>
  </div>
</ContentLayout>
